# 0002. Pin third-party plugins by commit, audit before bumping

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

Records an existing decision (accepted by the owner on 2026-11-11): third-party plugins only
change when I deliberately move their pinned commit after an audit.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: plugins run code and hooks with my permissions on every machine; a
  third-party repo can change at any time, and tracking its default branch would install
  those changes unreviewed.
- **Pinning**: each third-party entry in `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` has a `github`
  source with `repo` and a full 40-character `sha`: `ponytail` (`DietrichGebert/ponytail`)
  and `diagram-design` (`cathrynlavery/diagram-design`). Their `description` starts with
  "Third-party (...), pinned" so the list shows it.
- **Bumping**: a new `sha` lands only after `plugin-audit` on that commit. The audit
  (`plugins/workflow/skills/plugin-audit/audit.py`, read-only) lists what each plugin runs:
  hook commands, MCP servers, scripts; flags `npx`/`uvx`/`bunx`/`pnpx`/`pipx` packages with
  no version or `@latest`/`@next`, network calls (`fetch(`, `urlopen`, `curl`, `wget`,
  sockets) and credential access (`~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, `.netrc`, keychain, `*_TOKEN`,
  `*_SECRET`, `API_KEY`).
- **Same rule in CI**: GitHub Actions in `.github/workflows/check.yml` are pinned to commit
  SHAs (version in a comment), and the Claude Code CLI to an exact npm version.
- **Consequences**: no silent supply-chain changes; upstream fixes wait for a manual,
  audited bump.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: Claude Code marketplace `github` source with `sha`, `plugin-audit` skill.
- Alternatives: track the default branch: changes arrive unreviewed; vendor a copy: manual
  syncing, loses upstream history.
